  "id": "educational-neuroscience",
  "term": "educational neuroscience",
  "definition": "Educational neuroscience is an area of research that connects neuroscience with psychology and education to inform teaching and learning. In the school context, it focuses on translating findings about brain-related processes such as attention, executive functions, and neuroplasticity into educational applications and practice, often through collaboration between researchers and educators.",
